--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -4,12 +4,23 @@ A small team notes app. Next.js App Router + TypeScript + Tailwind.
 
 ## Status
 
-- Users live in `src/lib/users.ts` as an in-memory list.
-- `/dashboard` shows the current user and the team.
-- There is no sign-in, no billing, and no email yet.
+- Auth is [Better Auth](https://better-auth.com): email + password and Google sign-in.
+  Config in `src/lib/auth.ts`, endpoints at `/api/auth/*`, pages at `/sign-in` and `/sign-up`.
+- Users, sessions and linked accounts live in a SQLite file (`node:sqlite`, no native deps).
+  Tables are created automatically on first request; Ada and Grace are seeded.
+  On the very first boot Better Auth logs a one-off "Database schema mismatch" before the tables exist — harmless.
+- `src/lib/users.ts` reads users from that table; `getCurrentUser()` returns the signed-in user,
+  `requireUser()` redirects to `/sign-in` if there is none.
+- `/dashboard` is protected twice: `src/proxy.ts` bounces requests without a session cookie,
+  and the page itself validates the session via `requireUser()`.
+- There is no billing and no email yet (so no email verification or password reset).
 
 ## Develop
 
 ```bash
+cp .env.example .env.local   # then fill in BETTER_AUTH_SECRET and Google credentials
 npm run dev
 ```
+
+Google OAuth redirect URI: `http://localhost:3000/api/auth/callback/google`.
+Requires Node 22.13+ (for `node:sqlite`).
